iPadOS-Padpipa-6

This repository holds tooling (MIT, see LICENSE), per-unit configuration and documentation. It does not contain, and its
checks refuse, any Apple software, IPSW content, or proprietary firmware.

It builds from these projects, checked out at the commits pinned in manifest/sources.lock.toml, under their own licenses:

  UniXNU (BSD-2-Clause-Patent)               https://github.com/UniXNU/UniXNU
  UniXNU-pipa, xVanTuring (BSD-2-Clause-Patent; ShengPlatformPower.cpp MIT)
                                             https://github.com/xVanTuring/UniXNU-pipa
  uefi-pipa / Mu-Silicium (BSD-2-Clause-Patent; Binaries: proprietary vendor UEFI drivers)
                                             https://github.com/xVanTuring/uefi-pipa
  XNU, libpthread, corecrypto sources (APSL-2.0 and Apple's terms)
                                             https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions
  Mesa (MIT)                                 https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa

Consulted as references or donors (nothing copied unless a file header says so, with attribution):
  HakiOS (APSL-2.0 + MIT), MiCode Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource pipa-t-oss (GPL-2.0), LineageOS device and kernel trees
  (Apache-2.0 / GPL-2.0), UniXNU-j716f.

iPadOS is Apple's. The owner downloads the IPSW from Apple and uses it on their own device; this project does not
redistribute it, and Apple's services (activation, Apple ID, iCloud, App Store) are not a goal. This is an independent
research project, not affiliated with or endorsed by Apple, Xiaomi or Qualcomm.
